{
  "0": "Across all four categories, change only interest aggregation: use r_t=0.65*h_t+0.35*m_t, where m_t is the normalized causal exponential mean of valid encoder states with a five-item half-life. Apply at every supervised position and inference, excluding padding and future states. The previous 0.20 pooling weight improved validation; a stronger contribution may further stabilize recent interests. Preserve all other settings and synchronize the predictor writer. Train and load one model per category.",
  "1": "Across all four categories, change only feature construction: compute item occurrence counts from training interactions and scale each input item embedding by 1-0.15*log1p(count_i)/max_j(log1p(count_j)), leaving positional inputs unchanged. This fixed, bounded frequency feature may reduce domination by ubiquitous items while retaining their identity. Preserve learned embedding design, history selection, backbone, readout, scoring, loss and training settings. Save counts with each model and reproduce scaling in the predictor writer; use one model per category.",
  "2": "Across all four categories, change only the learning objective: retain the existing loss and add 0.2*mean(softplus(s_negative-s_positive)) over the same sampled positive/negative pairs at valid supervised positions. Explicit pairwise separation may improve HR@10 beyond independent label fitting. Preserve sampling, features, embeddings, backbone, readout, scoring, optimizer, scheduler, batches, epochs and seeds. Train and load exactly one model per category.",
  "3": "Across all four categories, change only interaction scoring: replace dot-product compatibility with sum_k(d_k*r_k*e_item,k), using one jointly learned diagonal vector d initialized to ones per category and shared across training positions and candidates. Dimension-specific compatibility may suppress noisy interest coordinates with little additional capacity. Preserve input features, embeddings, causal Transformer topology, history readout, loss and training settings. Update checkpoint loading and the predictor writer to use this same scorer; load one model per category."
}
